  "summary": "Toledo City Council voted 9-0 to authorize an independent audit of the city's use and oversight of Flock Safety ALPR cameras, examining how data is accessed, searched, shared, retained, and used. The cameras will remain operational during the audit; Mayor Kapszukiewicz said the city could turn them off if abuse is found. Police Chief Troendle supports the audit but opposes pausing the cameras.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Council voted 9-0 to request an independent audit of the city's use and oversight of the Flock system. The audit will examine how information is accessed, searched, shared, retained, and used.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "We won't fight the audit. We want our officers to be using the cameras in the correct way, and if someone is misusing our technology, we want to know about it.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Toledo Mayor Wade Kapszukiewicz confirmed after the meeting that the cameras would not be paused during the audit, but he said if the audit reveals abuse of the system, the city could turn them off.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
